SECURITY REVIEW OF app.js
==========================

## CRITICAL FINDINGS

### 1. MISSING AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (OWASP Top 10 #2: Broken Authentication)
SEVERITY: CRITICAL

ISSUE:
The /users endpoint exposes sensitive user data (names, emails) without any authentication or authorization checks. Any unauthenticated user can access this data.

CURRENT CODE:
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
```

RISKS:
- Unauthorized access to PII (Personally Identifiable Information)
- Data breach exposure
- Privacy regulation violations (GDPR, CCPA)
- No user identity verification

RECOMMENDATION:
Implement authentication middleware to verify user identity before exposing sensitive data.

REMEDIATED CODE:
```javascript
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

// Authentication middleware
function authenticateToken(req, res, next) {
  const authHeader = req.headers['authorization'];
  const token = authHeader && authHeader.split(' ')[1]; // Bearer token

  if (!token) {
    return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Access token required' });
  }

  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, user) => {
    if (err) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid or expired token' });
    }
    req.user = user;
    next();
  });
}

app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => {
  // Only return users if properly authenticated
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
```

