## HIGH PRIORITY FINDINGS

### 2. MISSING INPUT VALIDATION & SANITIZATION (OWASP Top 10 #1: Injection)
SEVERITY: HIGH

ISSUE:
While the current endpoints don't accept user input, the application lacks any input validation framework. If future endpoints are added that accept parameters (query, body, path), they will be vulnerable to injection attacks.

RISKS:
- SQL Injection (if database queries are later added)
- NoSQL Injection
- XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) attacks
- Command Injection
- Log Injection

RECOMMENDATION:
Implement input validation and sanitization using industry-standard libraries:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const { body, query, param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');
const mongoSanitize = require('mongo-sanitize');
const helmet = require('helmet');

const app = express();

// Middleware to sanitize inputs
app.use(mongoSanitize()); // Prevents NoSQL injection
app.use(helmet()); // Sets security headers

// Example: POST endpoint with validation
app.post('/users/:id', 
  param('id').isInt({ min: 1 }).toInt(),
  body('name').trim().isLength({ min: 1, max: 100 }).escape(),
  body('email').isEmail().normalizeEmail(),
  (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
    }
    // Process validated input
    res.json({ success: true });
  }
);
```

