## Security Checklist

### Before Production Deployment

- [ ] JWT_SECRET is set via environment variable (not hardcoded)
- [ ] All endpoints requiring auth have `authenticateToken` middleware
- [ ] Role-based access control implemented
- [ ] Sensitive data is filtered based on user role
- [ ] Input validation on all parameters (query, body, params)
- [ ] Rate limiting on authentication endpoints (max 5 attempts / 15 min)
- [ ] Security headers configured (helmet)
- [ ] CORS properly configured (not wildcard *)
- [ ] Error handling sanitized (no stack traces to client)
- [ ] HTTPS enforced in production
- [ ] Logging and monitoring configured
- [ ] Database uses parameterized queries
- [ ] Dependencies scanned for vulnerabilities (`npm audit`)
- [ ] Passwords hashed with bcrypt (if applicable)
- [ ] OWASP Top 10 reviewed and addressed
- [ ] Security testing completed (unit + integration)
- [ ] Code review completed
- [ ] WAF rules configured (if applicable)

---

## Deployment Security

### Environment Variables Required
```bash
NODE_ENV=production
JWT_SECRET=<generate-with-openssl>
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
LOG_LEVEL=warn
```

### Docker Security Best Practices
```dockerfile
FROM node:18-alpine
WORKDIR /app

# Don't run as root
USER node

# Install dependencies
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --only=production

# Copy application
COPY --chown=node:node . .

# Health check
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s CMD node healthcheck.js

EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "app.js"]
```

### Monitoring & Alerts
- Set up alerts for:
  - Failed login attempts (> 5 in 15 min)
  - Unauthorized access attempts
  - High error rate (> 5% of requests)
  - Unusual traffic patterns
  - Security header violations

