## Security Checklist

### Authentication & Authorization
- [ ] All endpoints require authentication or explicit public marking
- [ ] JWT tokens have reasonable expiration (not 30 years)
- [ ] Passwords are hashed with bcrypt (min 12 rounds)
- [ ] Sensitive operations require re-authentication
- [ ] Token refresh mechanism implemented
- [ ] Logout properly invalidates tokens
- [ ] CORS origins are explicitly whitelisted
- [ ] No hardcoded credentials in code

### Input Validation
- [ ] All user inputs are validated (query, body, params, headers)
- [ ] File uploads have size limits and allowed types
- [ ] URLs are validated and normalized
- [ ] Email validation includes normalization
- [ ] Integers have min/max bounds
- [ ] Strings have length limits
- [ ] Enums use whitelist, not blacklist

### Data Protection
- [ ] Sensitive data minimization (don't return unnecessary PII)
- [ ] Passwords never exposed in responses or logs
- [ ] Email addresses not logged unnecessarily
- [ ] Encryption for data at rest
- [ ] HTTPS enforced (not just available)
- [ ] Security headers present (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options)
- [ ] No sensitive data in URLs (use POST body instead)

### Error Handling
- [ ] Stack traces not exposed in production
- [ ] Generic error messages to users
- [ ] Detailed errors only in logs
- [ ] No information disclosure via error codes
- [ ] 404s for missing resources don't confirm existence

### Rate Limiting & DoS Protection
- [ ] Rate limiting on all public endpoints
- [ ] Stricter limits on auth endpoints
- [ ] Request size limits (JSON, URL-encoded)
- [ ] No infinite loops or expensive operations
- [ ] Database query timeouts set
- [ ] Caching implemented for expensive operations

### Logging & Monitoring
- [ ] Security events logged (auth failures, access denials)
- [ ] Failed requests logged
- [ ] Admin actions audited
- [ ] Logs stored securely (not world-readable)
- [ ] Log retention policy implemented
- [ ] No sensitive data in logs (passwords, tokens, PII)
- [ ] Alert system for suspicious activity

### Dependencies
- [ ] npm audit shows 0 vulnerabilities
- [ ] Dependencies kept up to date
- [ ] package-lock.json committed to version control
- [ ] No dev dependencies in production
- [ ] License compliance checked

### API Security
- [ ] API versioning for compatibility
- [ ] Request/response validation schemas
- [ ] Content-Type properly set
- [ ] X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
- [ ] X-Frame-Options prevents clickjacking
- [ ] X-XSS-Protection enabled
- [ ] Referrer-Policy configured

### Environment Configuration
- [ ] .env file not in version control
- [ ] .env.template provides documentation
- [ ] No secrets in environment variables for production
- [ ] Database credentials separate from code
- [ ] API keys stored in secure vault (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager)
- [ ] Feature flags don't expose sensitive functionality

