#### Development:
- [ ] Use .env.example (never commit .env)
- [ ] Add .env to .gitignore
- [ ] Use different secrets for dev vs production
- [ ] Never hardcode secrets
- [ ] Don't share .env files via email/chat

#### Staging:
- [ ] Use cloud secret manager
- [ ] Enable secret rotation
- [ ] Restrict access to staging secrets
- [ ] Enable audit logging
- [ ] Use separate credentials per environment

#### Production:
- [ ] Use enterprise vault (AWS/GCP/Azure)
- [ ] Enable secret rotation (30-90 days)
- [ ] Encrypt all secrets in transit
- [ ] Encrypt all secrets at rest
- [ ] Use IAM for access control
- [ ] Enable comprehensive audit trails
- [ ] No plaintext secrets in logs
- [ ] Monitor for unauthorized access
- [ ] Have incident response plan

#### Application Code:
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] No fallback secrets ('dev-secret')
- [ ] Fail fast if secrets missing
- [ ] Don't log secrets
- [ ] Rotate JWT signing keys regularly
- [ ] Validate secret strength
- [ ] Use strong encryption (minimum 256-bit keys)
- [ ] Implement secret versioning

