## Common Vulnerabilities & Quick Fixes

### 🔴 XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)
**Problem:** User input rendered as HTML
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG
res.send(`<h1>${userInput}</h1>`);

// ✅ RIGHT
query('name').escape(); // or .trim()
res.json({ name: userInput }); // JSON safe
```

### 🔴 SQL Injection
**Problem:** User input in SQL queries
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG
db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${req.query.id}`);

// ✅ RIGHT
query('id').isInt(); // Validate first
db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [req.query.id]);
```

### 🔴 Brute Force
**Problem:** No login attempt limits
```javascript
// ✅ RIGHT
app.post('/login', rateLimit({ max: 5 }), (req, res) => { ... });
```

### 🔴 CSRF
**Problem:** Forms can be submitted from other sites
```javascript
// ✅ RIGHT
const csrf = require('csurf');
app.use(csrf());
// Include token in forms
```

### 🔴 Information Disclosure
**Problem:** Stack traces shown to users
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG
res.send(err.stack);

// ✅ RIGHT
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
  res.json({ error: 'An error occurred' });
} else {
  res.json({ error: err.message, stack: err.stack });
}
```

